1
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:06,726
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>索納島
努布拉島西南87英里

2
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:24,209
<font color=#ff5000>侏儸紀公園2 失落的世界

3
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:37,638
Thank you so much. That looks fabulous.

4
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:39,432
Thank you, Geoffrey.

5
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:40,475
You're welcome.

6
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:43,853
We'll also take a bottle of red as well. Thank you.

7
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:45,021
Certainly.

8
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:48,024
Right, now...

9
00:01:48,358 --> 00:01:50,026
Thank you, Barry. You're welcome.

10
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,194
Thank you.

11
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:54,530
That looks wonderful. Beautiful day.

12
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:57,033
Where are you going?

13
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:58,159
To eat my sandwich.

14
00:01:58,243 --> 00:02:00,077
You'll ruin your appetite for prawns.

15
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:01,412
l don't like prawns.

16
00:02:01,497 --> 00:02:03,122
Darling, don't wander off.

17
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:06,375
For God's sake, leave her alone, Deirdre.

18
00:02:06,502 --> 00:02:08,294
Go play with your ball.

19
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,754
Don't be so annoying!

20
00:02:15,511 --> 00:02:18,888
Darling, what about snakes?

21
00:02:20,015 --> 00:02:22,517
There aren't any snakes on the beach.

22
00:02:22,601 --> 00:02:24,477
Just let her enjoy herself for once.

23
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,148
-Edward?   -Yes, ma'am.

24
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,142
Hello, there.

25
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:08,855
What are you, a little bird or something?

26
00:03:13,944 --> 00:03:17,864
Are you hungry? Take a bite. lt's roast beef.

27
00:03:18,282 --> 00:03:21,075
lt's good. Come on. l won't hurt you.

28
00:03:22,828 --> 00:03:26,137
Mommy! Daddy! You've got to come see this!

29
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,467
l found something!

30
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:43,097
Cathy, darling, lunch is ready!

31
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:47,018
Are you looking at this?

32
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:50,479
l'm afraid there isn't enough to go around.

33
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,236
Paul?

34
00:03:59,323 --> 00:04:00,531
Cathy?

35
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:06,370
Will you hurry up? Hurry up!

36
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,930
You're him, right?

37
00:05:07,391 --> 00:05:08,766
Excuse me?

38
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:12,228
The scientist? The guy? l saw you on TV.

39
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:16,732
l believed you.

40
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:51,267
Who shall l tell Mr. Hammond is calling?

41
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:54,186
Ian Malcolm. l've been summoned.

42
00:06:16,752 --> 00:06:18,210
Dr. Malcolm!

43
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:19,712
Oh, my God.

44
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:22,423
Hello, Dr. Malcolm.

45
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:24,008
Kids, kids.

46
00:06:24,134 --> 00:06:27,219
lt's so great to see you.

47
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:29,722
lt's so great. Look at you.

48
00:06:30,057 --> 00:06:31,599
You came to see Grandpa?

49
00:06:31,683 --> 00:06:34,935
Yeah, he called me. Do you know what it's about?

50
00:06:36,188 --> 00:06:39,815
l don't, either. This joint's kind of creepy, isn't it?

51
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,859
ls everything okay?

52
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,694
Well, not exactly.

53
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,124
Dr. Malcolm.

54
00:06:57,626 --> 00:07:01,796
Dr. Malcolm. Here to share a few campfire stories with my uncle?

55
00:07:07,803 --> 00:07:11,972
You can convince The Washington Post and SkepticaI Inquirer of what you want

56
00:07:12,057 --> 00:07:14,683
but l was there. l know what happened and so do you.

57
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:18,270
Do you actually believe that everyone who chose discretion did so

58
00:07:18,355 --> 00:07:21,524
for a nefarious motive? Even Lex and Tim?

59
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:24,360
Leave them out of it. lt's not a game.

60
00:07:24,477 --> 00:07:25,444
No.

61
00:07:25,979 --> 00:07:31,575
You signed a nondisclosure agreement before you went to the island that forbade you from discussing what you saw.

62
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,743
You violated that agreement.

63
00:07:32,828 --> 00:07:36,205
l did. And you lied about the deaths of three people.

64
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:38,165
You misinformed the public,

65
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,375
which made me look like a nut.

66
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:41,293
Hasn't been so good for my livelihood...

67
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:44,255
We made a generous compensatory offer for your injuries.

68
00:07:44,339 --> 00:07:45,840
A payoff and an insult.

69
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:48,300
When you spin reality, cover up evidence,

70
00:07:48,385 --> 00:07:50,678
it hurts more than my reputation.

71
00:07:50,762 --> 00:07:52,429
As l recall,

72
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:55,975
your university revoked your tenure

73
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:57,768
for your selling wild stories to the press.

74
00:07:57,853 --> 00:08:01,063
l didn't sell anything. l never took a cent, and l told the truth.

75
00:08:01,148 --> 00:08:02,439
Your version of it.

76
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:04,984
There aren't "versions" of the truth.

77
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:06,443
lnGen can't keep spewing out...

78
00:08:06,570 --> 00:08:09,071
lnGen is my responsibility now.

79
00:08:09,156 --> 00:08:11,073
l will jealously defend its interests.

80
00:08:11,158 --> 00:08:13,701
Your responsibility? What about Mr. Hammond?

81
00:08:14,995 --> 00:08:18,706
lt is our board of directors l must face, not my uncle.

82
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:22,376
Trust me, your problems are about to be rendered moot.

83
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:26,297
ln a few weeks' time, they'll be long forgotten.

84
00:08:28,383 --> 00:08:29,842
Not by me.

85
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:31,343
Careful.

86
00:08:33,805 --> 00:08:36,682
This suit cost more than your education.

87
00:08:38,476 --> 00:08:40,853
You were right and l was wrong. There!

88
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:43,939
Did you ever expect to hear me say such a thing?

89
00:08:45,442 --> 00:08:47,276
Thank God for Site B.

90
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:50,279
Site B?

91
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:53,282
lsla Nublar was just a showroom,

92
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:55,034
something for the tourists.

93
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:56,702
Site B was the factory floor.

94
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:59,997
That was on lsla Sorna, 80 miles from Nublar.

95
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,084
We bred the animals there, and nurtured them for a few months,

96
00:09:04,169 --> 00:09:06,503
then moved them into the park.

97
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:08,797
Really? l did not know that.

98
00:09:09,633 --> 00:09:11,759
After the accident in the park,

99
00:09:11,843 --> 00:09:15,471
Hurricane Clarissa wiped out our facility on Site B.

100
00:09:15,639 --> 00:09:17,514
Call it an act of God.

101
00:09:18,642 --> 00:09:23,687
We had to evacuate. The animals were released to mature on their own.

102
00:09:24,231 --> 00:09:28,442
"Life will find a way," as you once so eloquently put it.

103
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:31,779
By now we have a complete ecological system on the island

104
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:34,907
with dozens of species living in their own social groups

105
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:39,036
without fences, boundaries, or constraining technology.

106
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:40,996
And for four years...

107
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:45,209
l've tried to keep it safe from human interference.

108
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:49,935
That's right. Hopefully, you've kept the island quarantined and contained.

109
00:09:50,139 --> 00:09:53,259
But l'm in shock about all this.

110
00:09:53,343 --> 00:09:55,344
l mean, that they're still alive.

111
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:57,680
You bred them lysine-deficient.

112
00:09:57,847 --> 00:10:01,642
Shouldn't they have kicked after seven days without supplemental enzymes?

113
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:04,228
Yes! But, by God, they're flourishing.

114
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:07,523
That's one of 1,000 questions l want the team to answer.

115
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:08,732
Team?

116
00:10:08,817 --> 00:10:09,858
Yes.

117
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:14,697
l've organized an expedition to go in,

118
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:17,616
thank you, and document them.

119
00:10:17,701 --> 00:10:20,869
To make the most spectacular living fossil record

120
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:22,162
the world has ever seen.

121
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:25,582
Go in and document? You mean with people?

122
00:10:25,709 --> 00:10:29,211
Yes, the animals won't know they're there. Very low impact.

123
00:10:29,296 --> 00:10:32,089
Strictly observation and documentation.

124
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,258
Our satellite infrareds

125
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:37,303
show the animals are fiercely territorial.

126
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:40,806
The carnivores are isolated in the interior of the island

127
00:10:40,890 --> 00:10:43,434
so the team can stay on the outer rim.

128
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:47,438
Don't worry. l'm not making the same mistakes again.

129
00:10:47,564 --> 00:10:50,149
No, you're making all new ones.

130
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:55,446
John! So, there's another island with dinosaurs,

131
00:10:55,572 --> 00:11:02,745
no fences this time, and you want to send people in, very few people, on the ground, right?

132
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:06,248
Who are the four lunatics you're trying to con into this?

133
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:09,376
lt was difficult to convince them as to what they would see,

134
00:11:09,461 --> 00:11:12,004
in the end had to use my checkbook to get them there.

135
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:16,592
But there's Nick Van Owen, who is a video documentarian,

136
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:21,930
Eddie Carr, who's a field equipment expert.

137
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:25,601
We have our paleontologist

138
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:29,813
and l was hoping that perhaps you might be the fourth.

139
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:33,650
We've been on the verge of Chapter 1 1

140
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,611
ever since that accident in the park.

141
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:39,490
There are those in the company who wanted to exploit Site B

142
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:41,450
in order to bail us out.

143
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:43,577
They've been planning it for years,

144
00:11:43,661 --> 00:11:46,038
and l've been able to stop them until now.

145
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:48,348
But, a few weeks ago,

146
00:11:48,758 --> 00:11:50,376
a British family on a yacht cruise

147
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:53,057
stumbled across the island

148
00:11:53,763 --> 00:11:55,923
and their wee girl was injured.

149
00:11:56,758 --> 00:11:58,258
She's fine.

150
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:04,348
But the board has used the incident to take control of lnGen from me.

151
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:08,310
Now it's only a matter of time before this

152
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:11,647
lost world is found and pillaged.

153
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:16,402
Public opinion is the one thing l can use to preserve it,

154
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:18,404
but to rally that support

155
00:12:18,822 --> 00:12:24,535
l need a complete photo record of those animals alive and in their natural habitat.

156
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:28,372
So you went from capitalist to naturalist in just four years.

157
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:30,666
That's something.

158
00:12:33,378 --> 00:12:37,214
lt's our last chance at redemption.

159
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,177
John,

160
00:12:43,221 --> 00:12:44,430
no.

161
00:12:45,098 --> 00:12:47,224
Of course, no.

162
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:51,145
And l'm going to contact the other three members of your team

163
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:53,272
and stop them from going.

164
00:12:53,356 --> 00:12:55,691
Who's the paleontologist, by the way?

165
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:58,360
She came to me, l want you to know this.

166
00:12:59,446 --> 00:13:00,529
Who did?

167
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:03,991
Leave it to you, Ian, to have associations, affiliations,

168
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:07,327
even liaisons, with the best people in so many fields.

169
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:08,662
Not Sarah.

170
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:11,707
Paleontological behavior study is a new field,

171
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:13,459
and Sarah Harding is on that frontier.

172
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,586
Her theories on parenting and nurturing

173
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,963
amongst carnivores have framed the debate.

174
00:13:18,381 --> 00:13:19,465
What are you doing?

175
00:13:19,549 --> 00:13:20,883
Where's your phone?

176
00:13:24,304 --> 00:13:25,888
lt's too late.

177
00:13:26,639 --> 00:13:28,474
She's already there.

178
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:36,064
The others are meeting her in three days.

179
00:13:41,279 --> 00:13:44,406
You sent my girlfriend to this island alone?

180
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:48,202
"Sent" is hardly the word. She couldn't be restrained.

181
00:13:48,286 --> 00:13:50,204
She was already working in San Diego,

182
00:13:50,288 --> 00:13:52,331
doing some research at the animal park.

183
00:13:52,415 --> 00:13:54,917
lt's only a couple of hours' flight from there.

184
00:13:55,001 --> 00:14:01,757
She was adamant, absolutely adamant about, here you are, about making the initial foray by herself.

185
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:04,092
She thinks she's Dian Fossey.

186
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:06,261
"Observation without interference," she said.

187
00:14:06,346 --> 00:14:08,680
She went on and on. You know how it is.

188
00:14:08,765 --> 00:14:12,351
After you were injured in the park, she sought you out.

189
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:15,896
Then she went all the way to a hospital in Costa Rica

190
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:19,691
to ask somebody who she didn't even know if the rumors were true.

191
00:14:19,776 --> 00:14:22,611
lf you want to leave your name on something, fine.

192
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:26,114
But stop putting it on other people's headstones.

193
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:31,078
She'll be fine. She's spent years studying African predators.

194
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:34,790
Sleeping downwind and all. She knows what she's doing.

195
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:37,626
And, believe me, the research team will...

196
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:40,921
lt's not a research expedition anymore.

197
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:42,226
lt's a rescue operation

198
00:14:42,431 --> 00:14:44,049
and it's leaving now.

199
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:07,364
You can't shave three days off my deadline and expect to be ready.

200
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:09,783
l'm not supplied. l haven't tested any of this.

201
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:13,120
Why give her a satellite phone if it doesn't work? Why doesn't it?

202
00:15:13,204 --> 00:15:15,760
Could be solar flares, the satellite,

203
00:15:15,965 --> 00:15:16,707
or maybe she turned it off.

204
00:15:16,791 --> 00:15:20,294
l need half air on the tires. We're flying pressurized.

205
00:15:20,378 --> 00:15:21,587
Does she know how to use it?

206
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:25,799
You kidding? She's faxed me refinements on 50% of the plans for this stuff.

207
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:28,760
Don't do that. You got to baby it a little bit. Love it.

208
00:15:28,845 --> 00:15:29,970
l'll love it when it works.

209
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,805
lt'll work when you love it.

210
00:15:31,889 --> 00:15:32,889
You coming along?

211
00:15:32,974 --> 00:15:35,392
l don't usually, but l can't resist.

212
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,394
Thanks for the two-minute warning.

213
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:39,271
Nick Van Owen, this is Ian Malcolm.

214
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:40,772
Nick's our field photographer.

215
00:15:40,857 --> 00:15:42,524
How do you do?

216
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,151
You do wildlife photography?

217
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:46,236
Wildlife, combat, you name it.

218
00:15:46,321 --> 00:15:49,948
When l was with Nightline, l was in Rwanda, Chechnya, Bosnia.

219
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:52,784
l do volunteer work with Greenpeace once in a while.

220
00:15:52,869 --> 00:15:54,870
Greenpeace? What drew you there?

221
00:15:55,330 --> 00:15:56,538
Women.

222
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:59,166
80%  female, Greenpeace.

223
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:00,876
Noble.

224
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:04,671
Noble was last year. This year l'm getting paid.

225
00:16:04,756 --> 00:16:08,550
Hammond's check cleared, or l wouldn't go on this wild-goose chase.

226
00:16:09,052 --> 00:16:12,846
You're going to the only place in the world where the geese chase you.

227
00:16:13,765 --> 00:16:15,557
Dad! Dad!

228
00:16:17,935 --> 00:16:20,854
Kelly, my honey, you found it. What took you so long?

229
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,481
Sorry, l couldn't get a cab.

230
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:23,857
Sweetie, that's okay.

231
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:27,861
Listen, l've got to tell you something. l've got to talk to you.

232
00:16:29,072 --> 00:16:30,739
l don't even know this woman.

233
00:16:30,823 --> 00:16:33,033
You've known Karen for 1 0 years.

234
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:36,495
She doesn't even have Sega. She's such a troglodyte.

235
00:16:36,579 --> 00:16:38,705
Cruel, but good word use.

236
00:16:39,082 --> 00:16:41,041
Why can't l stay with Sarah?

237
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:44,127
She's out of town. Karen's fantastic.

238
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:47,172
She'll take you places. You'll have a fantastic time.

239
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:50,384
Stop saying "fantastic." Where are you going, anyway?

240
00:16:51,052 --> 00:16:56,724
lt's only for a few days.

241
00:16:52,061 --> 00:16:55,389
l wouldn't be going if it wasn't really important.

242
00:16:55,473 --> 00:16:56,848
l'm your daughter all the time.

243
00:16:56,933 --> 00:17:00,102
You can't abandon me whenever opportunity knocks.

244
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:03,188
That hurts my feelings. Your mom tell you to say that?

245
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:05,774
Dr. Malcolm, downstairs, please.

246
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:08,402
l know we've had some hard going.

247
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:12,114
But in the last few years, we've started to work things out.

248
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:14,700
Yeah, but crack on me a bit.

249
00:17:14,784 --> 00:17:16,660
Ground me or something. Send me to my room.

250
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:18,704
You never do any of that stuff.

251
00:17:18,788 --> 00:17:20,997
Why would l? You turned out so

252
00:17:21,124 --> 00:17:24,668
beautiful, brilliant, powerful, funny, and generous.

253
00:17:24,794 --> 00:17:26,878
The queen, goddess. My inspiration.

254
00:17:26,963 --> 00:17:28,171
Dr. Malcolm.

255
00:17:28,256 --> 00:17:31,925
l could come be your research assistant, like l was in Austin.

256
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:34,302
This is nothing like Austin.

257
00:17:35,805 --> 00:17:38,014
Anyway, you have your own stuff.

258
00:17:38,141 --> 00:17:41,393
Your gymnastics competition. You've been training for months.

259
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:42,936
Gymnastics?

260
00:17:43,146 --> 00:17:46,940
l scrubbed out, Dad, l got cut from the team. Thanks for knowing.

261
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:50,026
l'm sorry, honey.

262
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:53,321
l know how much that meant to you.

263
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:55,490
You like to have kids.

264
00:17:55,575 --> 00:17:58,076
But you just don't want to be with them, do you?

265
00:17:59,996 --> 00:18:03,081
lt wasn't me who dumped you and split for Paris,

266
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:04,708
so don't take it out on me.

267
00:18:05,168 --> 00:18:07,169
Dr. Malcolm, downstairs!

268
00:18:13,843 --> 00:18:16,094
Honey, l'm sorry. l'm sorry.

269
00:18:17,764 --> 00:18:20,638
You want some good parental advice?

270
00:18:20,649 --> 00:18:21,224
Don't listen to me.

271
00:18:24,854 --> 00:18:26,188
How are we doing here?

272
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:31,902
The specs say it can't deform at 1 2,000 PSl, so we just have to test it.

273
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:33,278
Let's clear. Are we clear?

274
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:34,571
What's this?

275
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:37,699
A High Hide.

276
00:18:38,409 --> 00:18:41,703
A High Hide. You know, you go up and hide, high.

277
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:43,955
lt goes up to where the trees are

278
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,875
and keeps the researchers out of harm's way.

279
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:50,879
Actually, it puts them at a very convenient biting height.

280
00:18:51,798 --> 00:18:53,465
What's the time? Do you have the time?

281
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:55,091
Do l have the time? Why?

282
00:18:55,176 --> 00:18:56,718
We're leaving in three hours.

283
00:19:16,239 --> 00:19:17,906
This is so cool.

284
00:19:37,226 --> 00:19:39,160
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(索納島)

285
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:21,011
Lindstradt air rifle. Fires a subsonic Fluger impact delivery dart.

286
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,596
lt works better than your satellite phone?

287
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,097
That's funny.

288
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:28,226
l loaded it with the enhanced venom of Conus Purpurascens, South Sea cone shell.

289
00:20:28,311 --> 00:20:30,312
Most powerful neurotoxin in the world.

290
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:31,730
Acts within 0.002 of a second.

291
00:20:31,814 --> 00:20:34,190
Which is faster than the nerve-conduction velocity.

292
00:20:34,275 --> 00:20:37,527
So the animal's down before it even feels the prick of the dart.

293
00:20:37,612 --> 00:20:38,862
ls there an antidote?

294
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:40,864
Like if you shot yourself in the foot?

295
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:42,449
Don't do that. You'd be dead before

296
00:20:42,533 --> 00:20:44,951
you even realized you had an accident.

297
00:20:49,123 --> 00:20:51,416
He says he's unloading us here.

298
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,918
He won't go further up the river.

299
00:20:53,002 --> 00:20:55,545
He's heard too many stories about this island chain.

300
00:20:55,630 --> 00:20:58,006
He'll drop us off and anchor offshore.

301
00:20:58,132 --> 00:20:59,758
What kind of stories?

302
00:21:05,723 --> 00:21:10,018
Stories of fishermen that came too close to the island and never returned.

303
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:13,688
He has a radio. He has a satellite phone.

304
00:21:16,692 --> 00:21:19,819
When you need him, call and he'll be here in two hours.

305
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:21,780
But he will not stay here.

306
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:26,201
He won't stay anywhere near these islands.

307
00:21:26,369 --> 00:21:29,537
They call the islands "Las Cinco Muertes"?

308
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:33,541
What does that mean?

309
00:21:35,169 --> 00:21:36,711
"The Five Deaths",

310
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,672
he says.

311
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:56,356
l put a location sensor in Dr. Harding's phone,

312
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:57,857
so we should get a reading.

313
00:21:57,942 --> 00:21:59,317
l'm so relieved.

314
00:21:59,402 --> 00:22:02,821
Don't push my buttons. We're almost on top of her dot.

315
00:22:02,905 --> 00:22:04,614
She should be around here.

316
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:06,950
Over there.

317
00:22:20,798 --> 00:22:22,048
Sarah!

318
00:22:22,391 --> 00:22:23,380
Sarah!

319
00:22:23,392 --> 00:22:24,723
Sarah!

320
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:26,469
Sarah Harding!

321
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:29,764
How many Sarahs do you think are on this island?

322
00:22:28,897 --> 00:22:31,297
Sarah...

323
00:22:40,943 --> 00:22:42,110
What?

324
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:45,822
Something big.

325
00:22:58,427 --> 00:23:00,622
天啊

326
00:23:00,838 --> 00:23:02,005
Wow.

327
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:19,147
This is magnificent.

328
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:22,692
Yeah. "Ooh, ah," that's how it always starts.

329
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:26,362
But then later there's running and screaming.

330
00:23:28,449 --> 00:23:29,616
Wow.

331
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:52,555
Nick!

332
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:58,311
l guess you got the jump on us, didn't you, Sarah?

333
00:23:58,395 --> 00:23:59,479
Yeah.

334
00:24:04,026 --> 00:24:08,071
Ian, l never thought in a million years Hammond could get you to come here.

335
00:24:10,825 --> 00:24:12,000
Hi, Eddie.

336
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:12,700
Hi, Sarah.

337
00:24:13,035 --> 00:24:16,371
Got a granola bar or something? l'm starving.

338
00:24:18,249 --> 00:24:20,041
Did you see those animals?

339
00:24:20,167 --> 00:24:24,504
A family group, a pair-bond and a sub-adult, long after the juvenile was nest bound.

340
00:24:24,588 --> 00:24:27,632
Every egg clutch l've seen has crushed, trampled shells.

341
00:24:27,716 --> 00:24:30,135
Hatchlings stay in the birth environment a long time.

342
00:24:30,219 --> 00:24:34,889
That's conclusive. l can put that controversy to rest if l get a shot of the nest.

343
00:24:35,224 --> 00:24:37,100
Have you been attacked?

344
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:40,728
No, that's my lucky pack. That's how it always looks.

345
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:44,274
Okay, Sarah...

346
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:46,262
-ls that a Nikon?   -Yes.

347
00:24:46,535 --> 00:24:50,238
Can l borrow that? l'll be right back, baby, l promise.

348
00:24:53,242 --> 00:24:56,661
When Hammond called you,

349
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:58,079
why didn't you say something to me?

350
00:24:58,372 --> 00:25:00,665
l knew you would have stopped me from coming.

351
00:25:00,749 --> 00:25:03,042
l would have tied you to the bed.

352
00:25:03,127 --> 00:25:05,503
l know how they survived without lysine.

353
00:25:05,588 --> 00:25:06,629
l don't care.

354
00:25:06,714 --> 00:25:09,382
The herbivore species that are thriving

355
00:25:09,466 --> 00:25:12,927
eat mostly agama beans, soy, anything lysine-rich.

356
00:25:13,262 --> 00:25:16,306
And the carnivores eat the herbivores, so...

357
00:25:18,309 --> 00:25:19,767
Wait.

358
00:25:21,395 --> 00:25:23,646
Stay there. Be quiet. l'll be right back.

359
00:25:23,731 --> 00:25:24,939
Sarah, No! No!

360
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:29,277
Stay there.

361
00:25:57,105 --> 00:25:58,163
Sarah,

362
00:25:59,808 --> 00:26:01,267
She's much too close.

363
00:26:01,352 --> 00:26:02,644
What the hell is she doing?

364
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:03,978
Too close.

365
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:28,878
She has to touch it. She can't not touch.

366
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:33,883
She's going right up to it. Once she sees something, she has to...

367
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:44,811
ls this even possible?

368
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:47,063
What?

369
00:26:48,732 --> 00:26:52,568
This? What did you think you'd document? What did you think you'd see?

370
00:26:52,695 --> 00:26:55,029
Animals. Maybe...

371
00:26:57,032 --> 00:26:58,574
big iguanas.

372
00:27:01,537 --> 00:27:02,745
Fruitcakes.

373
00:27:11,005 --> 00:27:13,548
They get very angry when you run out of film.

374
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:15,967
Sarah!

375
00:27:20,689 --> 00:27:21,519
Sarah!

376
00:27:24,018 --> 00:27:25,184
Shoot them!

377
00:27:25,269 --> 00:27:26,936
They're just protecting their baby.

378
00:27:27,021 --> 00:27:28,271
So am I!

379
00:27:49,877 --> 00:27:51,711
l think they're leaving.

380
00:27:59,386 --> 00:28:00,595
Wow.

381
00:28:00,929 --> 00:28:03,014
These images are incredible. Legendary.

382
00:28:03,098 --> 00:28:06,184
Guys shoot their whole life, they never get stuff half this good.

383
00:28:06,268 --> 00:28:09,145
Just give me the Pulitzer right now. Today, please.

384
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:13,524
The competition's over, close the entries, l'd like to thank everyone who lost.

385
00:28:13,609 --> 00:28:17,111
Don't light that! Dinosaurs pick up scents from miles away.

386
00:28:17,279 --> 00:28:20,073
We're here to observe and document, not interact.

387
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:22,950
Which, by the way, is a scientific impossibility.

388
00:28:23,077 --> 00:28:24,494
Heisenberg Uncertainty Principle.

389
00:28:24,578 --> 00:28:26,537
What you study, you also change.

390
00:28:26,622 --> 00:28:30,041
l'll risk it. l'm sick of scratching around in rock and bone

391
00:28:30,125 --> 00:28:32,877
making assumptions and deductions about

392
00:28:32,961 --> 00:28:34,045
the nurturing habits of animals

393
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:37,090
that have been dead for 65 million years. l'm sick of it, man.

394
00:28:37,174 --> 00:28:38,966
Then you fill my head with stories for four years.

395
00:28:39,051 --> 00:28:41,052
Of course l came down here.

396
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:42,845
Stories of mutilation and death.

397
00:28:42,930 --> 00:28:44,097
Weren't you paying attention?

398
00:28:44,181 --> 00:28:46,849
Please! Don't treat me like l'm a grad student.

399
00:28:46,934 --> 00:28:49,685
l've worked around predators since l was 20 years old.

400
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:52,313
Lions, jackals, hyenas, you.

401
00:29:00,364 --> 00:29:02,031
Where's the fire?

402
00:29:02,324 --> 00:29:05,284
l'm trying to change 100 years of entrenched dogma.

403
00:29:05,411 --> 00:29:09,163
Dinosaurs were characterized very early on as vicious lizards.

404
00:29:09,248 --> 00:29:12,667
There's great resistance to the idea of them as nurturing parents.

405
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:17,602
Robert Burke said the T. Rex was a rogue who abandoned its young at the earliest opportunity.

406
00:29:17,806 --> 00:29:19,424
I can prove otherwise.

407
00:29:19,508 --> 00:29:22,510
Fire! Dr. Malcolm, fire, base camp!

408
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:31,602
No! Water makes the smoke billow. Use dirt!

409
00:29:31,687 --> 00:29:33,604
Who started the fire?

410
00:29:34,982 --> 00:29:40,987
I just wanted to make dinner. I wanted it ready when you guys got back.

411
00:29:42,948 --> 00:29:45,825
Do you see any family resemblance there?

412
00:29:46,994 --> 00:29:48,786
You practically told me to come here.

413
00:29:48,871 --> 00:29:50,204
I... What?

414
00:29:50,706 --> 00:29:52,623
You said, "Don't listen to me."

415
00:29:52,708 --> 00:29:54,625
I thought you were trying to tell me something.

416
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:57,462
Kelly, you knew exactly what l meant. You have no...

417
00:29:57,546 --> 00:29:59,422
You want to lock her up for her curiosity?

418
00:29:59,506 --> 00:30:01,299
Where do you think she gets it?

419
00:30:01,383 --> 00:30:02,633
Thank you, Sarah.

420
00:30:02,718 --> 00:30:05,553
Don't start the teaming-up thing.

421
00:30:07,306 --> 00:30:10,850
Out of the conversation. Please. Really.

422
00:30:11,359 --> 00:30:12,849
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(你一直待在拖車裏？)

423
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:11,343
Eddie?

424
00:30:12,100 --> 00:30:12,643
What?

425
00:30:12,728 --> 00:30:15,313
Why in the hell doesn't this thing ever work?

426
00:30:15,397 --> 00:30:18,816
lt's not a landline. You're not in a phone booth.

427
00:30:18,901 --> 00:30:21,110
You got to wait for a decent signal.

428
00:30:20,869 --> 00:30:21,995
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(訊號，好吧)

429
00:30:23,489 --> 00:30:26,991
Violence and technology, not good bedfellows.

430
00:30:28,327 --> 00:30:33,289
Hammond wants your equipment as close to the animals as possible.

431
00:30:33,499 --> 00:30:36,918
Great idea. And why don't you smear on a little sheep's blood?

432
00:30:37,211 --> 00:30:41,172
Eddie, is there any reason to think the radio in the trailer might work?

433
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:42,757
Don't tease me.

434
00:30:42,925 --> 00:30:46,552
lf you feel qualified, try flicking the switch to "on."

435
00:30:47,930 --> 00:30:50,890
Okay, l'm taking my daughter out of here.

436
00:30:51,099 --> 00:30:54,352
Anyone coming with me, this is your last chance to get out.

437
00:30:54,436 --> 00:30:56,771
When you're out in the field...

438
00:30:57,022 --> 00:30:59,774
Nick, if you're staying, l'll gladly deliver

439
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:01,359
a letter to your wife or loved one

440
00:31:01,443 --> 00:31:03,277
so you can say goodbye.

441
00:31:03,445 --> 00:31:06,447
Eddie, if you have any personal effects

442
00:31:06,532 --> 00:31:09,534
it's the least l can do. l'll be in there, guys.

443
00:31:09,618 --> 00:31:12,286
Our presence needs to be 100% antiseptic.

444
00:31:12,412 --> 00:31:14,872
lf we so much as bend a blade of grass...

445
00:31:14,957 --> 00:31:16,040
Dad, are you mad?

446
00:31:16,124 --> 00:31:17,917
No, l'm not mad. l'm furious.

447
00:31:19,545 --> 00:31:21,504
What is this? This looks like your room.

448
00:31:21,588 --> 00:31:22,588
l was going to clean it up.

449
00:31:22,673 --> 00:31:24,090
Right now.

450
00:31:25,425 --> 00:31:28,553
What is this? There are 100 switches!

451
00:31:28,637 --> 00:31:32,640
Don't be mad. l was going to call to let you know where l was.

452
00:31:32,808 --> 00:31:34,809
l always do, don't l?

453
00:31:35,102 --> 00:31:39,903
l'm the best kind of girlfriend there is. One who travels a lot.

454
00:31:39,948 --> 00:31:41,950
You like that, right?

455
00:31:41,950 --> 00:31:46,737
You love your independence. l've gotten used to being apart, but that's not how l want to live.

456
00:31:46,989 --> 00:31:49,754
Kelly, this is tall talk.

457
00:31:49,958 --> 00:31:51,858
Just for a minute.

458
00:31:51,743 --> 00:31:54,662
lt's like a height restriction at an amusement park.

459
00:31:55,455 --> 00:31:57,431
lf you wanted to rescue me,

460
00:31:57,465 --> 00:32:02,336
why didn't you bail me out from that museum fundraiser three weeks ago, like you said you would?

461
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:06,173
This is a slightly different situation.

462
00:32:06,300 --> 00:32:09,844
What about the dinner with your parents you never showed up for?

463
00:32:09,970 --> 00:32:12,680
Why not rescue me when l really need it?

464
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:14,849
Be there when you say you will?

465
00:32:15,100 --> 00:32:18,519
l have made a career out of waiting for you.

466
00:32:18,854 --> 00:32:21,105
You know, Sarah has a pretty good...

467
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:23,441
lt's so important to your future that you not finish that sentence.

468
00:32:23,525 --> 00:32:25,776
Please, outside!

469
00:32:27,529 --> 00:32:30,197
Ian, come on. Look.

470
00:32:32,492 --> 00:32:36,370
l love that you rode in here on a white horse. l really do.

471
00:32:37,706 --> 00:32:40,958
lt's very touching, very dramatic.

472
00:32:41,543 --> 00:32:44,712
l just need you to show up in a cab every once in a while, too.

473
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:47,798
What are you doing? Don't go out there. lt's not safe.

474
00:32:47,883 --> 00:32:50,801
Stay in here. Come back. Shut the door.

475
00:32:55,223 --> 00:32:56,390
Okay.

476
00:32:57,726 --> 00:33:01,479
l know what l'm doing. You guys should definitely go.

477
00:33:02,481 --> 00:33:04,148
But l'm going to stay.

478
00:33:04,733 --> 00:33:08,069
l love you. l just don't need you right now.

479
00:33:09,571 --> 00:33:12,698
What you need is a good anti-psychotic.

480
00:33:13,075 --> 00:33:15,159
l'll be back in five or six days.

481
00:33:15,243 --> 00:33:16,827
No, you'll be back in five or six pieces.

482
00:33:16,912 --> 00:33:20,164
What bothers you is that l'm not afraid of this place, and you are.

483
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:24,168
Of course l am. That's the whole thing. All l want is...

484
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,753
What's that sound?

485
00:33:35,764 --> 00:33:38,474
Here we go. l'll get you out on one of these, now.

486
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:40,267
Hello! Over here!

487
00:33:43,605 --> 00:33:47,441
l don't get it. lt says lnGen on the side of that chopper!

488
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:51,570
l don't get that. Why would Hammond send two teams?

489
00:33:53,699 --> 00:33:55,574
Cut the umbilical, Dad!

490
00:33:55,951 --> 00:33:59,078
Doesn't he trust us? We haven't even started.

491
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:13,050
This is as good a place as any for base camp. That's first priority after we're finished.

492
00:34:13,135 --> 00:34:17,096
l want it up and running in 30 minutes. That's half an hour.

493
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:18,556
Understood? Over.

494
00:34:18,640 --> 00:34:19,890
Cancel that order.

495
00:34:20,392 --> 00:34:21,809
What? Why?

496
00:34:21,977 --> 00:34:23,644
This is a game trail, Mr. Ludlow.

497
00:34:23,729 --> 00:34:25,396
Carnivores hunt on game trails.

498
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:28,232
You want to set up base camp or a buffet?

499
00:34:31,737 --> 00:34:35,156
Let's find a new spot, shall we? Over and out.

500
00:34:35,449 --> 00:34:39,493
Peter, if l run your little camping trip, there are two conditions.

501
00:34:39,745 --> 00:34:42,830
First, l'm in charge. lf l'm not around, Dieter is.

502
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:45,833
You just pay us, tell us we're doing well,

503
00:34:45,917 --> 00:34:47,835
and serve us Scotch after a good day.

504
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:50,838
Second condition, my fee. You can keep it.

505
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:54,842
All l want for my services, is the right to hunt a tyrannosaurus.

506
00:34:54,968 --> 00:34:57,762
A male. A buck only. How and why are my business.

507
00:34:57,846 --> 00:35:00,598
lf you don't like those conditions, you're on your own.

508
00:35:00,682 --> 00:35:03,017
So go ahead, set up base camp here,

509
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:06,228
in a swamp, or in the middle of a Rex nest for all l care.

510
00:35:06,354 --> 00:35:09,190
l've had too many safaris with rich dentists

511
00:35:09,274 --> 00:35:11,275
to listen to any more suicidal ideas.

512
00:35:11,485 --> 00:35:12,693
Okay?

513
00:35:14,362 --> 00:35:15,488
Okay.

514
