Eddie, you all right?

776
01:01:47,287 --> 01:01:48,496
Yeah. l'm coming.

777
01:01:48,789 --> 01:01:51,499
We need the rope. Throw it down here. Hurry up!

778
01:01:51,625 --> 01:01:54,168
Good throw. Did you tie this to anything?

779
01:01:58,757 --> 01:02:01,467
We're sliding down!

780
01:02:15,816 --> 01:02:17,274
Up you go.

781
01:03:35,896 --> 01:03:38,063
Eddie! Hey!

782
01:03:59,952 --> 01:04:00,941
Come on!

783
01:04:31,034 --> 01:04:32,117
Go.

784
01:04:32,953 --> 01:04:34,787
lncrease your rate of climb.

785
01:05:44,640 --> 01:05:46,505
該死，該死

786
01:05:58,654 --> 01:05:59,746
我的天

787
01:06:56,930 --> 01:06:59,598
Our communication equipment's been destroyed.

788
01:06:59,766 --> 01:07:03,727
And if your radio and satellite phone were in those trailers...

789
01:07:03,812 --> 01:07:04,853
They were.

790
01:07:04,938 --> 01:07:06,271
Then we're stuck here.

791
01:07:06,439 --> 01:07:08,857
And stuck together, thanks to you people.

792
01:07:08,942 --> 01:07:11,694
We came to watch. You came to strip-mine the place.

793
01:07:11,778 --> 01:07:12,820
Back off.

794
01:07:12,904 --> 01:07:14,113
At least we came prepared.

795
01:07:14,564 --> 01:07:15,565
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>準備充分？你在說什麼？

796
01:07:14,280 --> 01:07:17,866
Five years of work and electrified fence

797
01:07:17,951 --> 01:07:18,992
couldn't prepare the other island.

798
01:07:19,160 --> 01:07:21,245
You think your Marlboro men will help?

799
01:07:21,329 --> 01:07:24,665
You're looters. You came to take. You have no rights.

800
01:07:24,749 --> 01:07:27,376
An extinct animal brought back to life has no rights.

801
01:07:27,460 --> 01:07:28,877
lt exists because we made it.

802
01:07:28,962 --> 01:07:30,754
We patented it. We own it.

803
01:07:32,090 --> 01:07:33,590
You looking for a problem?

804
01:07:33,675 --> 01:07:35,134
And l found you, didn't l?

805
01:07:35,593 --> 01:07:36,927
Stop!

806
01:07:38,304 --> 01:07:39,763
Come on!

807
01:07:39,848 --> 01:07:43,976
l know you. You're that Earth First bastard.

808
01:07:44,269 --> 01:07:45,394
What's Earth First?

809
01:07:45,478 --> 01:07:46,520
Professional saboteurs.

810
01:07:46,604 --> 01:07:48,021
Environmentalists! Criminals.

811
01:07:48,106 --> 01:07:49,857
Knock it off! Listen to me.

812
01:07:49,941 --> 01:07:52,151
Moving the baby to our camp may have

813
01:07:52,235 --> 01:07:53,736
changed the adults' perceived territory.

814
01:07:53,820 --> 01:07:55,028
Their what?

815
01:07:55,447 --> 01:07:57,990
That's why they attacked the trailers.

816
01:07:58,158 --> 01:07:59,867
They're defending this entire area now.

817
01:07:59,951 --> 01:08:01,660
We have to move now.

818
01:08:01,786 --> 01:08:06,081
To where? Our boat and their airlift are waiting for orders we can't send.

819
01:08:06,166 --> 01:08:07,624
All right.

820
01:08:07,709 --> 01:08:11,962
There's a communications center here near the old operations building.

821
01:08:12,046 --> 01:08:14,089
Everything ran on geothermal power.

822
01:08:14,174 --> 01:08:16,175
lt was never meant to need replenishing.

823
01:08:16,509 --> 01:08:19,845
lf we can get here, we can send a radio call to the airlift.

824
01:08:20,180 --> 01:08:21,430
You know the frequency?

825
01:08:21,514 --> 01:08:22,806
Here in this book.

826
01:08:23,016 --> 01:08:24,266
We'll mind those.

827
01:08:24,350 --> 01:08:25,517
How far is the village?

828
01:08:25,852 --> 01:08:27,561
A day's walk, maybe more.

829
01:08:31,232 --> 01:08:32,441
That's not the problem.

830
01:08:32,525 --> 01:08:33,650
What is?

831
01:08:34,986 --> 01:08:36,528
What is the problem?

832
01:08:37,405 --> 01:08:38,697
Velociraptors.

833
01:08:44,204 --> 01:08:48,540
Their nesting sites are in the island's interior, which is why

834
01:08:48,875 --> 01:08:50,501
we were keeping to the outer rim.

835
01:08:50,585 --> 01:08:52,127
Wait. What's a Veloc...

836
01:08:52,212 --> 01:08:55,172
Velociraptor. Carnivore. Pack hunter.

837
01:08:55,882 --> 01:08:57,925
Two meters tall, long snout,

838
01:08:58,218 --> 01:09:02,221
binocular vision, strong dexterous forearms, killing claws on both feet.

839
01:09:02,597 --> 01:09:04,473
The Rexes may track us, too,

840
01:09:04,557 --> 01:09:07,267
if they feel we're a threat to them or their infant.

841
01:09:07,352 --> 01:09:10,521
No, we'll lose them once we leave their territory.

842
01:09:10,680 --> 01:09:11,908
Don't bet on it.

843
01:09:12,181 --> 01:09:14,817
Tyrannosaur has the largest proportional olfactory cavity

844
01:09:14,901 --> 01:09:17,736
of any creature in fossil record, except one.

845
01:09:17,904 --> 01:09:18,904
Right.

846
01:09:19,364 --> 01:09:22,825
The turkey vulture could scent up to 1 0 miles.

847
01:09:22,909 --> 01:09:27,454
Right. This is all very thrilling, but l say we should head for the village.

848
01:09:27,580 --> 01:09:29,915
We could head back down to the lagoon.

849
01:09:30,041 --> 01:09:31,599
And sit out in the open,

850
01:09:32,201 --> 01:09:36,088
next to a heavily used water source hope that your captain comes back?

851
01:09:36,172 --> 01:09:37,798
He won't. He knows better.

852
01:09:37,882 --> 01:09:42,135
Then we head for the village, we might find shelter and we can call for help.

853
01:09:42,220 --> 01:09:44,805
Rex just fed, so he won't stalk us for food.

854
01:09:44,931 --> 01:09:46,682
Just fed? You mean Eddie?

855
01:09:47,216 --> 01:09:49,726
Show some respect. He saved our lives by giving his.

856
01:09:49,811 --> 01:09:51,478
Then his troubles are over.

857
01:09:51,604 --> 01:09:54,356
My point is predators don't hunt when they're not hungry.

858
01:09:54,440 --> 01:09:55,691
No, only humans do.

859
01:09:55,775 --> 01:09:57,025
You're breaking our heart.

860
01:09:57,110 --> 01:09:59,945
Saddle up! Let's get this moveable feast underway.

861
01:10:17,463 --> 01:10:18,964
Excuse me, cowboy.

862
01:10:20,466 --> 01:10:21,967
You want some gum?

863
01:10:24,470 --> 01:10:28,098
You seem like you have common sense. Why the hell are you here?

864
01:10:29,809 --> 01:10:33,228
Somewhere on this island is the greatest predator that ever lived.

865
01:10:33,313 --> 01:10:36,023
The second greatest predator must take him down.

866
01:10:36,149 --> 01:10:37,482
You going to use that?

867
01:10:37,567 --> 01:10:39,151
lf he doesn't surrender, yes.

868
01:10:39,444 --> 01:10:40,200
Let me see it.

869
01:10:40,269 --> 01:10:41,194
No.

870
01:10:43,156 --> 01:10:46,742
The animal exists for the first time in tens of millions of years

871
01:10:46,826 --> 01:10:49,786
and the only way you can express yourself is to kill it.

872
01:10:49,871 --> 01:10:52,915
Remember that chap about 20 years ago? l forget his name.

873
01:10:52,999 --> 01:10:56,209
Climbed Everest without any oxygen. Came down nearly dead.

874
01:10:56,336 --> 01:10:59,171
They asked him, "Why did you go up there to die?"

875
01:10:59,380 --> 01:11:02,174
He said, "l didn't. l went up there to live."

876
01:11:07,388 --> 01:11:09,514
l didn't wish you luck on your new venture.

877
01:11:09,599 --> 01:11:11,266
You're off to a promising start.

878
01:11:11,351 --> 01:11:14,353
My team is intact. l'm sorry for the loss of your man.

879
01:11:14,520 --> 01:11:18,690
lt's easy to criticize someone who generates an idea, assumes the risk.

880
01:11:18,816 --> 01:11:21,818
When you try to sound like Hammond, it comes off as a hustle.

881
01:11:21,903 --> 01:11:25,155
lt's not your fault. They say talent skips a generation.

882
01:11:25,573 --> 01:11:28,200
l'm sure your kids will be sharp as tacks.

883
01:11:28,534 --> 01:11:31,536
Hammond's reach exceeded his grasp. Mine does not.

884
01:11:31,913 --> 01:11:33,789
Taking dinosaurs off this island

885
01:11:33,873 --> 01:11:37,751
is the worst idea in the long, sad history of bad ideas.

886
01:11:37,877 --> 01:11:40,379
And l'll be there when you learn that.

887
01:11:55,728 --> 01:11:56,853
Go.

888
01:12:14,414 --> 01:12:16,540
Take a break. Five minutes.

889
01:12:28,761 --> 01:12:30,137
Are you injured?

890
01:12:32,765 --> 01:12:37,394
No, it's the baby's. l set its broken leg. lt won't dry in the humidity.

891
01:12:37,478 --> 01:12:39,646
Roland, a word?

892
01:12:41,274 --> 01:12:43,608
l'd love to know where we are.

893
01:12:48,823 --> 01:12:50,824
Making friends with Ahab?

894
01:13:06,174 --> 01:13:08,550
Carter, l'm going to the ladies' room.

895
01:13:08,885 --> 01:13:11,136
Wait for me here. Okay?

896
01:13:54,964 --> 01:13:56,295
天哪

897
01:14:01,521 --> 01:14:03,897
lt's not polite to sneak up on people.

898
01:14:24,377 --> 01:14:27,712
Carter! Where are you?

899
01:14:32,593 --> 01:14:34,594
Hey, Carter! l got turned around in here.

900
01:14:37,056 --> 01:14:38,098
Shit!

901
01:14:39,183 --> 01:14:41,893
Carter, let me hear from you!

902
01:14:49,235 --> 01:14:50,902
Hey, Carter!

903
01:15:06,419 --> 01:15:07,919
Hey, Carter!

904
01:15:41,570 --> 01:15:42,594
Carter!

905
01:15:49,078 --> 01:15:50,602
Carter!

906
01:16:36,676 --> 01:16:38,134
Roland!

907
01:16:44,016 --> 01:16:46,142
Okay, break's over. Moving on!

908
01:16:54,360 --> 01:16:55,568
Carry me.

909
01:16:56,195 --> 01:16:57,529
l got it.

910
01:16:58,906 --> 01:16:59,842
Carter.

911
01:17:00,649 --> 01:17:01,908
Carter.

912
01:17:15,164 --> 01:17:16,290
Roland!

913
01:17:23,672 --> 01:17:24,696
Roland!

914
01:17:27,184 --> 01:17:28,393
Get off!

915
01:18:29,413 --> 01:18:31,206
When did you last see him?

916
01:18:31,290 --> 01:18:32,624
10, 15 minutes.

917
01:18:35,169 --> 01:18:38,463
Come with me. And you. lf he's alive, we'll find him.

918
01:18:38,964 --> 01:18:40,882
The rest of you keep right on.

919
01:18:40,966 --> 01:18:44,135
Ten minutes, you'll reach the ridge. Wait for us there.

920
01:18:44,753 --> 01:18:49,224
No one tells the little girl.

921
01:18:54,647 --> 01:18:57,816
Right. Let's carry on.

922
01:19:00,486 --> 01:19:02,487
Everybody up.

923
01:19:04,156 --> 01:19:05,824
Come on. Up, up.

924
01:19:07,326 --> 01:19:10,161
All right, guys, let's get the hell out of here.

925
01:19:12,873 --> 01:19:13,957
Come on.

926
01:19:47,700 --> 01:19:49,033
Roland?

927
01:20:02,047 --> 01:20:03,506
Did you find him?

928
01:20:08,220 --> 01:20:09,998
Just the parts they didn't like. Map.

929
01:20:10,339 --> 01:20:10,930
地圖

930
01:20:14,351 --> 01:20:18,104
The operations building is right down in there

931
01:20:18,564 --> 01:20:21,483
about a mile and a half from the base of these cliffs.

932
01:20:21,567 --> 01:20:22,650
How do you know that?

933
01:20:22,735 --> 01:20:23,776
l've seen it.

934
01:20:24,445 --> 01:20:26,404
The climb down won't be easy.

935
01:20:27,781 --> 01:20:30,241
We'll let them sleep one more hour.

936
01:20:31,785 --> 01:20:33,119
Then we hit it.

937
01:21:23,712 --> 01:21:25,213
Oh, no.

938
01:22:42,207 --> 01:22:43,416
What is that?

939
01:23:03,011 --> 01:23:08,232
Kelly. Kelly.

940
01:23:19,745 --> 01:23:21,913
Stay down! Don't move!

941
01:23:22,414 --> 01:23:23,790
Don't run!

942
01:23:32,007 --> 01:23:34,092
Don't look, just run! Run!

943
01:23:49,441 --> 01:23:50,525
Bastard!

944
01:24:23,592 --> 01:24:25,321
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(警告！動物麻醉劑)

945
01:25:29,208 --> 01:25:30,708
You son of a bitch!

946
01:25:30,876 --> 01:25:32,126
He can't reach you!

947
01:25:32,211 --> 01:25:33,544
Stay back!

948
01:25:35,380 --> 01:25:36,798
He can't reach us!

949
01:25:37,049 --> 01:25:38,216
No!

950
01:25:48,852 --> 01:25:52,230
Oh, my God! A snake! Help me!

951
01:25:52,564 --> 01:25:53,815
Stay back!

952
01:26:06,537 --> 01:26:07,662
lt's okay. lt's okay.

953
01:26:08,580 --> 01:26:10,039
lt's coming back!

954
01:26:13,919 --> 01:26:15,127
Dad!

955
01:26:17,172 --> 01:26:18,506
Thank you.

956
01:26:31,144 --> 01:26:33,521
Don't go into the long grass!

957
01:26:39,194 --> 01:26:41,529
Not into the long grass!

958
01:27:02,968 --> 01:27:04,010
Move it.

959
01:27:04,678 --> 01:27:06,053
Keep moving.

960
01:27:08,640 --> 01:27:09,807
Move it!

961
01:27:40,339 --> 01:27:41,505
Hey, hey!

962
01:27:44,801 --> 01:27:46,052
Look at this.

963
01:27:46,470 --> 01:27:47,595
What is it?

964
01:27:47,679 --> 01:27:48,804
l think it's Ajay's bag.

965
01:27:54,803 --> 01:27:55,735
什麼？

966
01:28:05,113 --> 01:28:06,302
Go,

967
01:28:06,815 --> 01:28:07,698
as fast as you can.

968
01:28:09,117 --> 01:28:10,326
Go!

969
01:28:12,821 --> 01:28:14,482
Go! Go!

970
01:28:42,067 --> 01:28:43,776
l see structures there.

971
01:28:44,903 --> 01:28:48,572
They said the communications center is in the operations building.

972
01:28:48,657 --> 01:28:52,410
l'll get in there and send the radio call. See you there.

973
01:28:52,494 --> 01:28:54,161
Wait for us. Every second counts.

974
01:28:54,246 --> 01:28:56,414
lf you can keep up, you're welcome to try.

975
01:28:56,498 --> 01:28:57,790
Okay, here we come.

976
01:28:57,874 --> 01:28:59,125
No! Rest.

977
01:29:36,404 --> 01:29:39,669
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(侏羅紀公園)

978
01:29:46,715 --> 01:29:47,965
Oh, man.

979
01:29:50,919 --> 01:29:56,323
這是什麼？

980
01:30:35,964 --> 01:30:40,162
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(緊急供電系統)

981
01:31:02,374 --> 01:31:03,624
Damn it!

982
01:31:05,710 --> 01:31:06,919
Be there.

983
01:31:09,214 --> 01:31:13,134
CQ, this is lnGen Operations Harvest Leader to Harvest Base.

984
01:31:13,260 --> 01:31:18,722
Repeating, l'm calling for lnGen Operations Harvest Leader seeking lnGen Harvest Base.

985
01:31:18,807 --> 01:31:20,141
Go ahead, Harvest Leader.

986
01:31:20,225 --> 01:31:22,726
The operation has suffered severe casualties.

987
01:31:22,811 --> 01:31:24,979
The survivors are now in mortal danger.

988
01:31:25,063 --> 01:31:27,148
l need you to send rescue immediately.

989
01:31:27,315 --> 01:31:29,817
Our co-ordinates here are

990
01:31:30,152 --> 01:31:34,071
9 degrees 58 minutes north, 85 degrees...

991
01:32:25,457 --> 01:32:26,624
Nick!

992
01:32:30,078 --> 01:32:30,737
Nick!

993
01:32:33,581 --> 01:32:34,605
Nick!

994
01:32:38,720 --> 01:32:40,221
Nick Van Owen?

995
01:32:44,092 --> 01:32:44,751
Nick!

996
01:33:08,833 --> 01:33:10,000
Here, here!

997
01:33:11,544 --> 01:33:13,003
lnside! Anywhere!

998
01:33:15,257 --> 01:33:16,548
Come inside!

999
01:35:18,296 --> 01:35:19,546
Go.

1000
01:35:19,631 --> 01:35:21,173
Where do l go when l'm out?

1001
01:35:21,257 --> 01:35:22,758
l'm right behind you...

1002
01:35:49,577 --> 01:35:50,828
Look out!

1003
01:35:51,162 --> 01:35:52,329
Watch out!

1004
01:35:54,666 --> 01:35:55,999
Up here!

1005
01:36:07,512 --> 01:36:08,720
Kelly, no!

1006
01:36:21,192 --> 01:36:22,359
Hey, you!

1007
01:36:42,964 --> 01:36:44,965
The school cut you from the team?

1008
01:36:45,049 --> 01:36:45,833
Get out of here! Go!

1009
01:36:45,833 --> 01:36:47,926
Get out of here! Go!

1010
01:38:08,800 --> 01:38:10,300
Come on. Let's go!

1011
01:38:13,096 --> 01:38:14,972
Let's go!

1012
01:38:36,327 --> 01:38:37,995
Let's go!

1013
01:38:38,162 --> 01:38:39,788
What about the other survivors?

1014
01:38:39,872 --> 01:38:41,456
Another chopper's coming.

1015
01:38:53,461 --> 01:38:56,362
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(國際遺傳公司)

1016
01:39:00,685 --> 01:39:02,769
lt's okay. lt's over now.

1017
01:39:04,564 --> 01:39:07,566
That's one souvenir they won't be taking with them.

1018
01:39:16,367 --> 01:39:18,285
Find the infant tyrannosaur.

1019
01:39:18,453 --> 01:39:20,078
Roland can show you where the nest is.

1020
01:39:20,163 --> 01:39:21,705
l want it on my jet.

1021
01:39:22,123 --> 01:39:25,250
l'll take it directly to the infirmary in San Diego.

1022
01:39:25,918 --> 01:39:30,505
Hurry. l want to be airborne before the female knows we're here.

1023
01:39:33,000 --> 01:39:34,226
Roland?

1024
01:39:34,927 --> 01:39:36,219
Roland?

1025
01:39:37,305 --> 01:39:39,056
You probably saved lnGen.

1026
01:39:39,265 --> 01:39:41,725
We lost everything we came after on this trip.

1027
01:39:41,809 --> 01:39:44,936
But this animal and its infant will bail us out.

1028
01:39:45,229 --> 01:39:46,605
Congratulations.

1029
01:39:47,190 --> 01:39:50,484
You've got your trophy! A buck only.

1030
01:39:51,277 --> 01:39:56,239
But it's alive! Everyone will line up and appreciate it and what you did for us.

1031
01:39:57,742 --> 01:39:59,201
What's the matter?

1032
01:39:59,452 --> 01:40:01,495
He didn't make it. Ajay.

1033
01:40:02,830 --> 01:40:04,081
l'm sorry.

1034
01:40:05,124 --> 01:40:06,750
Really, l am.

1035
01:40:10,630 --> 01:40:12,923
l remember the people who've helped me.

1036
01:40:13,007 --> 01:40:15,717
There's a job for you in San Diego, if you want it.

1037
01:40:15,802 --> 01:40:17,135
No, thank you.

1038
01:40:19,430 --> 01:40:22,182
l've spent enough time in the company of death.

1039
01:40:36,072 --> 01:40:37,197
Oh, my God.

1040
01:41:26,614 --> 01:41:29,879
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(國際遺傳公司)

1041
01:41:38,301 --> 01:41:40,927
Fifteen years ago, John Hammond had a dream.

1042
01:41:41,637 --> 01:41:46,183
Like John himself, the dream was grand. lt was outsized. lt was bold.

1043
01:41:46,267 --> 01:41:49,269
lt was impractical. lt was not to be.

1044
01:41:49,979 --> 01:41:51,730
But half an hour from now,

1045
01:41:51,814 --> 01:41:55,150
John Hammond's dream, re-imagined, will come true.

1046
01:41:56,027 --> 01:42:00,197
For .01 of the cost of building a destination resort thousands of miles away...

1047
01:42:01,073 --> 01:42:02,866
ls this the Ludlow affair?

1048
01:42:02,950 --> 01:42:05,035
lt's private property. We're on the list.

1049
01:42:05,119 --> 01:42:06,703
Turn around, get back in your car.

1050
01:42:06,788 --> 01:42:08,288
This is Dr. Harding, l'm Dr. Malcolm.

1051
01:42:08,372 --> 01:42:10,707
We have Mr. Ludlow's test results.

1052
01:42:10,792 --> 01:42:12,000
There's good and bad news.

1053
01:42:12,627 --> 01:42:15,337
Tonight we will christen Jurassic Park, San Diego,

1054
01:42:15,421 --> 01:42:21,092
with a mega-attraction that will drive turnstile numbers to rival any theme park in the world.

1055
01:42:25,056 --> 01:42:29,559
l want to thank each one of you for coming in these wee small hours of the morning.

1056
01:42:30,645 --> 01:42:31,937
The ship is here.

1057
01:42:32,021 --> 01:42:33,230
lt's early?

1058
01:42:34,607 --> 01:42:36,149
You better come now.

1059
01:42:38,152 --> 01:42:39,569
lt's so exciting!

1060
01:42:41,572 --> 01:42:42,823
See that couple?

1061
01:42:42,907 --> 01:42:44,074
Sir, you need to look at this.

1062
01:42:44,158 --> 01:42:45,158
Let them see this up close.

1063
01:42:45,243 --> 01:42:46,243
Yes, sir.

1064
01:42:46,869 --> 01:42:48,328
Let me check.

1065
01:42:48,913 --> 01:42:52,040
l want a direct line to the Coast Guard right now.

1066
01:42:52,708 --> 01:42:56,169
Look. That's their transponder signal, Venture 5888.

1067
01:42:56,921 --> 01:42:58,588
They're coming in, but l can't raise them.

1068
01:42:58,673 --> 01:42:59,881
Try again.

1069
01:43:01,175 --> 01:43:05,470
Skipper, SS Venture, this is lnGen Harbor Master. Do you copy? Over.

1070
01:43:07,890 --> 01:43:13,103
Skipper, SS Venture, you are approaching the breakwater at flank speed. Reduce at once. Over.

1071
01:43:28,035 --> 01:43:30,412
SS Venture, reduce your speed at once.

1072
01:43:30,496 --> 01:43:34,958
SS Venture, this is lnGen Harbor Master. You are entering a docking area.

1073
01:43:35,793 --> 01:43:37,627
What's everybody looking at?

1074
01:43:41,924 --> 01:43:43,675
We should've stayed in the damn car.

1075
01:44:36,604 --> 01:44:38,104
You okay, Mr. Ludlow?

1076
01:44:38,189 --> 01:44:39,689
l don't know. How do l look?

1077
01:44:46,405 --> 01:44:47,697
Go up this one.

1078
01:45:12,390 --> 01:45:13,390
Oh, my God.

1079
01:45:13,474 --> 01:45:14,516
Where's the crew?

1080
01:45:16,477 --> 01:45:17,978
All over the place.

1081
01:45:28,572 --> 01:45:30,281
l smell a fuel leak!

1082
01:46:07,319 --> 01:46:11,448
Check the cargo hold! There may be crew down there.

1083
01:46:11,532 --> 01:46:12,907
Everybody off the boat!

1084
01:46:20,958 --> 01:46:22,667
No! Get away from that!

1085
01:46:56,494 --> 01:46:58,203
Now you're John Hammond.

1086
01:47:02,449 --> 01:47:05,213
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(不准帶入蔬果或動物)

1087
01:47:28,609 --> 01:47:30,276
Why wasn't it tranquilized?

1088
01:47:30,361 --> 01:47:32,821
lt was, with two darts of Carfentanil.

1089
01:47:32,905 --> 01:47:34,114
lt was over 1 0 milligrams.

1090
01:47:34,198 --> 01:47:35,406
That'd put it in a coma.

1091
01:47:35,491 --> 01:47:38,284
lt stopped breathing. We gave it naltrexone to counteract.

1092
01:47:38,369 --> 01:47:39,577
But we didn't know how much.

1093
01:47:39,662 --> 01:47:42,288
You gave an antagonist without knowing the dosage?

1094
01:47:42,373 --> 01:47:45,250
You put it in a narcoleptic state. lt's a locomotive now.

1095
01:47:45,334 --> 01:47:46,459
We're prepared here.

1096
01:47:46,544 --> 01:47:48,253
Any more dinosaurs on the boat?

1097
01:47:48,337 --> 01:47:50,004
No, we brought the infant back on the plane.

1098
01:47:50,089 --> 01:47:52,382
We had this to tranquilize it.

1099
01:47:56,679 --> 01:47:58,388
Do you have the infant?

1100
01:48:00,182 --> 01:48:01,349
lt's safe.

1101
01:48:04,395 --> 01:48:05,353
Ian.

1102
01:48:05,437 --> 01:48:08,481
The animal's dehydrated. First, it'll go to a water source

1103
01:48:08,566 --> 01:48:10,859
then look for the next thing its body needs.

1104
01:48:10,943 --> 01:48:15,572
All the containment equipment is here. We got to get it to the dock. The boat might be seaworthy.

1105
01:48:15,656 --> 01:48:17,323
l know what you're gonna say.

1106
01:48:17,408 --> 01:48:19,951
When we brought the baby to the trailer, it came.

1107
01:48:20,035 --> 01:48:23,454
There's no reason why it won't do the same thing here.

1108
01:48:24,832 --> 01:48:25,999
Yep.

1109
01:48:28,169 --> 01:48:29,669
Where's the infant?

1110
01:48:32,798 --> 01:48:34,883
ln a secured facility. Why?

1111
01:48:38,262 --> 01:48:39,846
Where's the facility?

1112
01:50:04,682 --> 01:50:06,891
There's a dinosaur in our backyard.

1113
01:50:13,440 --> 01:50:15,400
Benjamin, what are you doing?

1114
01:50:15,609 --> 01:50:17,110
What are you doing?

1115
01:50:17,945 --> 01:50:19,112
What?

1116
01:50:20,114 --> 01:50:23,074
Come on. There's a dinosaur in our backyard.

1117
01:50:23,242 --> 01:50:25,118
The problem is, you need to read to him.

1118
01:50:25,202 --> 01:50:26,286
No.

1119
01:50:26,370 --> 01:50:27,829
l will tell you what it is.

1120
01:50:27,913 --> 01:50:30,581
You have to serve him dinner, he won't be up all night.

1121
01:50:30,666 --> 01:50:32,417
lt's the stupid fish tank!

1122
01:50:32,501 --> 01:50:33,751
He needs a proper nightlight.

1123
01:50:33,836 --> 01:50:35,044
Put something over it!

1124
01:50:35,129 --> 01:50:36,713
lt may as well be daytime.

1125
01:50:36,797 --> 01:50:38,339
Just turn it off.

1126
01:50:52,179 --> 01:50:53,203
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(國際遺傳公司)

1127
01:50:59,945 --> 01:51:01,904
Slow down. Slow it down!

1128
01:51:26,013 --> 01:51:27,263
There it is.

1129
01:51:34,104 --> 01:51:39,088
He's sedated. Really heavily.

1130
01:51:39,793 --> 01:51:40,943
Give me a hand.

1131
01:51:44,281 --> 01:51:48,451
When the adult sees us again with his baby, isn't he going to be like:

1132
01:51:48,535 --> 01:51:49,619
"You!"

1133
01:51:50,788 --> 01:51:54,290
There may be some angry recognition.

1134
01:51:55,834 --> 01:51:58,795
Who knows? He may be just happy to see us.

1135
01:51:59,630 --> 01:52:01,631
What the hell are you doing?

1136
01:52:03,300 --> 01:52:04,842
We're taking the kid.

1137
01:52:05,719 --> 01:52:08,513
lf you really want to stop us, shoot us.

1138
01:52:10,391 --> 01:52:11,849
How will we find the adult?

1139
01:52:11,975 --> 01:52:13,476
Follow the screams.

1140
01:52:39,920 --> 01:52:42,505
Get to the other side of the bus!

1141
01:53:34,266 --> 01:53:34,999
There.

1142
01:53:35,408 --> 01:53:36,142
Oh, my God.

1143
01:53:50,032 --> 01:53:53,993
lt's too drugged. He won't know we have it unless it makes some sound!

1144
01:53:54,077 --> 01:53:56,412
Wake up. Come on.

1145
01:54:04,421 --> 01:54:05,505
He knows.

1146
01:54:21,438 --> 01:54:23,314
Ian, slow down a little.

1147
01:54:25,442 --> 01:54:26,817
l don't think so.

1148
01:54:37,971 --> 01:54:39,768
{\a6}<font color=#ffff00>(聖地牙哥市捕狗大隊)

1149
01:54:47,089 --> 01:54:49,215
This guy's almost fully awake.

1150
01:54:49,299 --> 01:54:50,591
You know where you're going?

1151
01:54:50,884 --> 01:54:54,554
Yeah, the waterfront's on the other side of these warehouses.

1152
01:54:54,638 --> 01:54:56,222
ls there a way through?

1153
01:54:56,306 --> 01:54:57,807
God. There could be.

1154
01:55:03,981 --> 01:55:05,147
There we go.

1155
01:55:08,026 --> 01:55:09,819
You have to follow me now.

1156
01:55:09,903 --> 01:55:11,153
There we go.

1157
01:55:12,030 --> 01:55:13,573
Got him? Yep.

1158
01:55:13,949 --> 01:55:15,324
Here we go.

1159
01:55:15,409 --> 01:55:16,409
Ready?

1160
01:55:16,493 --> 01:55:18,494
Where's the Rex? ls it behind us?

1161
01:55:26,753 --> 01:55:27,962
There's the water.

1162
01:55:28,046 --> 01:55:30,673
Shoot it. Tell them to shoot it.

1163
01:55:35,345 --> 01:55:39,849
No, you idiot, the adult. Shoot the adult. l want the baby back alive.

1164
01:56:09,546 --> 01:56:11,005
Dr. Malcolm!

1165
01:56:12,758 --> 01:56:15,468
What have you done with it? l want that infant!

1166
01:56:47,000 --> 01:56:48,334
Are you there?

1167
01:57:19,116 --> 01:57:20,491
There you are.

1168
01:57:40,721 --> 01:57:41,929
Wait.

1169
01:57:45,158 --> 01:57:47,820
Wait...

1170
01:57:53,166 --> 01:57:54,690
Wait.

1171
01:57:58,671 --> 01:58:02,607
Wait.

1172
01:59:51,268 --> 01:59:54,937
There's a first-rate shot of the ship's deck

1173
01:59:55,021 --> 02:00:01,944
and the cargo hold that, for the moment, contains the animal itself, presumably with the infant alongside.

1174
02:00:02,487 --> 02:00:07,116
By our calculations, they should be nearing the halfway point of this trip.

1175
02:00:07,200 --> 02:00:09,368
Jim, can you still hear me there?

1176
02:00:10,036 --> 02:00:13,080
Yes, I can, Bernard. We are halfway to the island.

1177
02:00:13,164 --> 02:00:16,500
lt is 206 nautical miles from our present location.

1178
02:00:16,626 --> 02:00:18,460
The ship is moving at 20 knots

1179
02:00:18,545 --> 02:00:21,839
which will put it in at about 11:30 a.m., Eastern time.

1180
02:00:21,965 --> 02:00:25,342
One of the Navy's primary concerns has been safety.

1181
02:00:25,552 --> 02:00:28,846
lf we look at the ever-growing escort around the ship

1182
02:00:29,014 --> 02:00:32,808
they're taking no chances of a repeat of the San Diego incident.

1183
02:00:33,435 --> 02:00:39,690
Let's take a moment to run the tape of our interview earlier today with John Hammond.

1184
02:00:39,858 --> 02:00:42,818
He's the former head of InGen Bio-Engineering,

1185
02:00:42,986 --> 02:00:45,696
the man who is now spearheading this movement

1186
02:00:45,822 --> 02:00:51,160
not only to return the animals to their island but to keep the island itself intact.

1187
02:00:52,203 --> 02:01:00,210
lt is absolutely imperative that we work with the Costa Rican Department of Biological Preserves

1188
02:01:00,337 --> 02:01:06,967
to establish a set of rules for the preservation and isolation of that island.

1189
02:01:08,428 --> 02:01:13,265
These creatures require our absence to survive,

1190
02:01:13,350 --> 02:01:14,683
not our help.

1191
02:01:15,352 --> 02:01:22,191
And if we could only step aside and trust in nature

1192
02:01:23,318 --> 02:01:25,694
life will find a way.

1193
02:01:57,410 --> 02:02:00,402
導演：史蒂芬·史匹柏

1194
02:02:01,914 --> 02:02:04,815
編劇：大衛·柯比

1195
